  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a date-only due date in a negative-UTC-offset zone, when bucketed by useKanbanColumns and scored by todoScoring, then both agree on the calendar day (the kanbanParity tz test passes).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Exactly one parseDueDate implementation exists across SmartTodo.Components and Spaarke.UI.Components.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the locked weights/formula region of todoScoring.ts is byte-identical to master.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A pull request against master is open, ready for review, with the item ids in its body.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the PR contains no package-lock.json changes and no file outside this task's scope.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The after-change test run has no failure that is absent from the master baseline run.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <completion date="2026-10-03">PR #1118 (47cc95987). SmartTodo 68 to 73 tests, all pass; UI.Components scoped run 182 to 188, all pass. Finding: the todoScoreMappings sha256 guard was ALREADY RED on master (pinned 2026-08-16; todoScoring.ts then changed by 8737dea124, smart-todo-r5 UAT #6, without a re-pin). Main session inspected 8737dea124: it changed a header comment, parseDueDate and computeDueLabel label text only; the weights/composite-formula region is untouched, so the re-pin blesses a reviewed change. No blocking CI check caught the red guard for seven weeks. Shared stash stack verified untouched after the agent used git stash.</completion>
  <notes>Merge this PR FIRST: it is a live user-facing bug, and on-branch task 081 (C-13) reuses the calendar-days helper in dateLocal.ts rather than writing a second one.</notes>

